W:In the bleak midwinter frosty wind made moan,
W:Earth stood hard as iron, water like a stone;
W:Snow had fallen, snow on snow, snow on snow,
W:In the bleak midwinter, long a go.
W:
W:(Christina Rosetti, 1872)

